---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="CloudOps Guard"
  description="CloudOps Guard is a read-only auditing tool for Kubernetes and GitLab CI/CD. Explore interactive Kubernetes and GitLab demos, or open your own report.json in the local report explorer -- entirely in your browser."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <p class="status-label status-label--neutral">Web foundation preview</p>
      <h1>CloudOps Guard</h1>
      <p class="hero__lede">
        Read-only auditing for Kubernetes and GitLab CI/CD &mdash; built to find
        reliability, security, and cost issues without ever writing to the systems it
        audits.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="capabilities-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 id="capabilities-heading">Released capabilities</h2>
      <p class="section__intro">
        These two audits are implemented today, as a command-line tool you run
        yourself against your own cluster or project.
      </p>
      <div class="card-grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Kubernetes audit</h3>
          <p>
            Reviews namespaces, pods, deployments, and replica sets for missing
            resource requests/limits, mutable image tags, and excessive container
            restarts.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>GitLab CI/CD audit</h3>
          <p>
            Reviews a single GitLab project's branch protection, merge-request
            policy, CI/CD settings, and job/service image references.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--muted" aria-labelledby="read-only-heading">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h2 id="read-only-heading">Read-only, by design</h2>
      <p>
        CloudOps Guard only ever reads. It never modifies, creates, patches, or
        deletes a resource in an audited system, never retrieves Secret or ConfigMap
        contents, and never collects container environment variable values,
        application logs, or GitLab CI/CD variables.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="milestone-heading">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <p class="status-label status-label--neutral">Current web milestone</p>
      <h2 id="milestone-heading">Interactive Web Demo and Local Report Explorer</h2>
      <p>
        This site lets visitors explore CloudOps Guard's Kubernetes and GitLab checks
        with synthetic example data, and open a <code>report.json</code> file the CLI
        already produced &mdash; entirely inside their own browser, with the file
        never uploaded anywhere.
      </p>
      <p>
        Two interactive demonstrations are implemented, each using two fixed synthetic
        scan states for the same fictional target &mdash; search, filter, sort, and
        inspect findings, compare the earlier state to the later one to see
        new/persistent/resolved findings, and switch to a deterministic executive
        summary, entirely in your browser. The local report explorer opens one or two
        <code>report.json</code> files the CLI already produced &mdash; also never
        uploaded anywhere &mdash; and offers the same search/filter/sort/comparison/
        executive-summary experience. A searchable check catalogue, other product
        pages, and a contact form all arrive in later implementation phases. This site
        has not been deployed, released, or published.
      </p>
      <p class="index-cta-group">
        <a class="cta" href="/demo/kubernetes">Explore Kubernetes &rarr;</a>
        <a class="cta" href="/demo/gitlab">Explore GitLab &rarr;</a>
        <a class="cta" href="/explorer">Open Local Report Explorer &rarr;</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--muted" aria-labelledby="preview-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 id="preview-heading">A preview of the visual language</h2>
      <p class="section__intro">
        These are illustrative design examples only &mdash; not results from a real or
        synthetic audit.
      </p>
      <div class="card-grid" aria-label="Illustrative severity label examples">
        <div class="card preview-card">
          <p class="status-label status-label--critical">Critical</p>
          <p class="preview-card__caption">Example severity label</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card preview-card">
          <p class="status-label status-label--high">High</p>
          <p class="preview-card__caption">Example severity label</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card preview-card">
          <p class="status-label status-label--medium">Medium</p>
          <p class="preview-card__caption">Example severity label</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card preview-card">
          <p class="status-label status-label--low">Low</p>
          <p class="preview-card__caption">Example severity label</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="roadmap-heading">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h2 id="roadmap-heading">What comes next</h2>
      <p>
        The interactive <a href="/demo/kubernetes">Kubernetes</a> and
        <a href="/demo/gitlab">GitLab</a> demonstrations, browser-side report
        comparison and an executive summary view, and the
        <a href="/explorer">local report explorer</a> are the first of these to be
        implemented. Later phases add: a searchable catalogue of every implemented
        check, other product pages, and a separate, isolated contact form. Full
        screen-reader/WCAG accessibility review and a broader browser test matrix are
        also still to come. None of these other pieces exist on this site yet, and
        this site has not been deployed, released, or published.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding-block: var(--space-2xl) var(--space-xl);
  }

  .hero__lede {
    font-size: var(--font-size-md);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    max-width: 38rem;
  }

  .section__intro {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    max-width: 42rem;
  }

  .index-cta-group {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .card-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-md);
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
  }

  .preview-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-2xs);
  }

  .preview-card__caption {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
</style>
